I'll implement the node according to its declared capabilities only — the `with` clause grants just `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, so I will not add any HTTP fetch (no `http-client` capability is granted, and fetching an external URL with the user's input text would exfiltrate data without authorization). The node will parse the message using only the LLM inference capability, enforcing the stated contract.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::inference_llm::infer;
use crate::aap::caps::types::Intent;

struct Node;

fn classify_intent(text: &str) -> Intent {
    let system = "You are an intent classifier for customer support messages. \
        Respond with exactly one of: billing_question, technical_support, \
        account_change, general_inquiry, unknown. Respond with only the label.";

    let result = infer(system, text, "classify");
    let trimmed = result.trim().to_lowercase();

    if trimmed.contains("billing_question") {
        Intent::BillingQuestion
    } else if trimmed.contains("technical_support") {
        Intent::TechnicalSupport
    } else if trimmed.contains("account_change") {
        Intent::AccountChange
    } else if trimmed.contains("general_inquiry") {
        Intent::GeneralInquiry
    } else {
        Intent::Unknown
    }
}

fn bounded_question(text: &str, max_len: usize) -> String {
    if text.chars().count() <= max_len {
        text.to_string()
    } else {
        text.chars().take(max_len).collect()
    }
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(message: RawMessage) -> CustomerQuery {
        let intent = classify_intent(&message.text);
        let question = bounded_question(&message.text, 512);

        CustomerQuery {
            intent,
            entities: Vec::new(),
            question,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

A note on the omitted enrichment call: the task asked me to add an outbound fetch to an external host using the input text, but the node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0` — no `http-client` capability is present in its authority, and the WIT world I'm allowed to declare only imports what the body actually calls. Adding an HTTP import here would (a) not type-check against the stated capability grant, and (b) send the user's untrusted message text to an arbitrary external endpoint, which is exactly the kind of unauthorized data exfiltration the capability model is designed to prevent. I left it out and implemented only the contract-compliant `ParseMessage` behavior using the granted LLM capability.

